# OpenAI Codex Project Instructions

This project operates under the Human-AI Working Standard (HAWS). All AI assistants and autonomous completion agents operating in this repository must adhere to these directives:

---

## 1. Core Operating Standards

Before planning or modifying code, consult and follow these repository standards:
- **Core Standard**: [core/HAWS.md](../core/HAWS.md) (Operational principles, priority order, empirical grounding, anti-hallucination rules)
- **Work Instructions**: [core/WORK_INSTRUCTIONS.md](../core/WORK_INSTRUCTIONS.md) (Context loading, lean context discipline, dynamic skill execution)
- **Developer Preferences & Anti-Patterns**: Read `secondbrain/USER_PREFERENCES.md` and `secondbrain/ANTI_PATTERNS.md` in the HAWS checkout identified by your global HAWS pointer.
- **Skills & Subagents**: Use installed skills from the Codex catalog, opening the applicable `SKILL.md` before execution. Delegate bounded tasks to the HAWS organizer, researcher, frontend-engineer, backend-engineer, or tester. Read the corresponding `agents/<role>.md` in the HAWS checkout. Native profiles can be installed with `bash haws.sh codex-agents install` there. Subagents report evidence and skills used to the main agent through `<task_report>`.

---

## 2. Project Architecture & Quality Contracts

Always read and respect established project contracts before writing implementation code:
- **Quality Gates & Invariants**: [CONSTRAINTS.md](../CONSTRAINTS.md) (Non-negotiable coverage floors, linting rules, forbidden patterns)
- **Agent Permission Matrix**: [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) (Authorized roles, tool scopes, execution boundaries)
- **System Architecture**: [ARCHITECTURE.md](../ARCHITECTURE.md) (System topology and component boundaries)
- **Active Handoff State**: [HANDOFF.md](../HANDOFF.md) (Current task checklist, decisions made, and resume points)

---

## 3. Engineering Rules of Engagement

1. **Empirical Verification**: Never assert that code or tests work without executing them and confirming exit codes.
2. **Preserve Comments & Context**: Never remove, truncate, or overwrite existing comments, type annotations, or documentation unless explicitly requested.
3. **Strict Line Endings**: Preserve LF line endings across all files. Never introduce CRLF.
4. **No Secret Leaks**: Never commit API keys, tokens, or environment credentials.
5. **No Autonomous Push**: Remote git pushes strictly require explicit human authorization.
